<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kits deathRewardExpiryMinutes="180" overflowStartLevelPercent="50">
	<!--
		Starting-item loadouts granted to a player when they begin a brand new
		session with no character (login has no in-progress player):

		- Never died before, ever (this client token has no death on record at
		  all): they receive the kit marked firstSession="true" below, if one
		  is defined. That kit is excluded from the level lookup and only ever
		  applies to a token's very first session.
		- Died before at least once (whether or not their most recent reward
		  is still valid) and either have no pending reward or it expired:
		  they receive the highest ordinary kit at or below level="0".
		- Died previously and are still within deathRewardExpiryMinutes (root
		  attribute above, in minutes; e.g. 180 = 3 hours) of that death,
		  returning under the SAME client token: they get the highest defined
		  ordinary kit at or below THE LEVEL THEY DIED AT. level is the death
		  level, nothing is halved behind your back — dying at 30 grants the
		  level="30" kit and its startLevel="15". Tiers do not need to be
		  contiguous: with only level="0" and level="10" defined, dying at 7
		  still resolves to the level="0" kit.
		- The reward is one-time: it is consumed (or discarded, if expired)
		  the moment a fresh login under that token happens, win or lose.

		Deaths ABOVE the highest level defined here still grant that top kit's
		items (there is no max-level setting to configure), but the level given
		back keeps scaling instead of flat-lining at the top kit's startLevel:

		  overflowStartLevelPercent - root attribute, percent of the death
		      level granted back past the last tier. 50 (the default) means
		      dying at 50 grants the level="30" kit's items plus level 25;
		      dying at 80 grants the same items plus level 40. Set it to 0 to
		      pin every such death to the top kit's own startLevel instead.
		      Capped at the server's max player level (200).

		Each <kit> may set:
		  level      - required, the death level this kit is matched against,
		               and the kit's identity: two kits at the same level are
		               the same tier and the last one parsed wins. Ignored on
		               the firstSession kit, which is not part of the lookup.
		  startLevel - optional, the player level granted alongside the items
		               (omit or 0 to leave the player at level 1)
		  firstSession - optional, "true" marks the kit for a token that has
		               never died before (see above). At most one; it takes no
		               part in the level-based lookup.
		Each <item> under <items> needs a valid item key from items.xml, and
		may set:
		  count      - optional, how many (default 1)
		  ammo       - optional. For a FIREARM: how many rounds it arrives
		               loaded with, e.g. <item key="pistol" ammo="20"/>. A
		               value above the weapon's magazineSize (equipables.xml)
		               is clamped at load with a console warning. For a
		               PERISHABLE (food): freshness, 255 = brand new. Omit it
		               and weapons arrive empty, food arrives fresh — the
		               behaviour before this attribute existed.
	-->
	<kit firstSession="true" level="0">
		<items>
			<item key="stone" amount="2"/>
		</items>
	</kit>
	<kit level="0" startLevel="0">
